nats-hub is licensed by path. Different parts of this repository are under
different licenses:

  * Client side (MCP server and plugins, Python workers and bridges, the
    Rust client library and client CLIs, installers): Apache License 2.0.
    Full text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt

  * Server side (hub-server, hub-admin and the code and assets only they
    run): Business Source License 1.1, with an Additional Use Grant that
    allows production use except offering it to others as a hosted service.
    Each version converts to Apache License 2.0 four years after its first
    public release.
    Full text and parameters: LICENSES/BUSL-1.1.txt

LICENSING.md says which paths fall under which license, in plain language.
REUSE.toml holds the same mapping in machine-readable form
(https://reuse.software).

